 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Hands for «وأصلحوا ذات بينكم» (after the Name), a book for «آياته», coins for spending, growth for «درجات». No motif on the Prophet ﷺ (5). Paradise (4:10-11) only named in the gloss, nothing drawn. STAGING v4: c1 (1: the question about the spoils of Badr, put to the Prophet) and c3 (5: his going out from his house to Badr) stay ambient: battle context and his own conduct; nobody is drawn. c2 (2-4): believers seated in a prayer hall by day; they lower their heads in awe right after the Name (2:7, hearts trembling); a book plate for the verses recited to them (2:10-14, ending before 2:16) and a soft sparkle for the faith that increases (2:13); they raise their hands on 2:17 (reliance on their Lord, both tafsirs). They pray on 3:2-3:4 (stand, ruku, sujud; no plate over the prayer), stand up and hand a purse to a poor man who comes in on 3:5 (3:6, spending: both tafsirs name obligatory and voluntary charity); he raises his hands on 4:1. 4: a growth plate for the high degrees (4:6, ending before 4:8); the noble provision (Paradise, Al-Muyassar) is not drawn and gets no plate; the camera stays on the believers."
 },
